h government, more specifically the division Geestkracht, for research in mental health care</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.zonmw.nl"/></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>GGZ Nederland</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ggznederland.nl/links/ggz/index.html"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wiebe</surname><given-names>EF</given-names></name><name><surname>Eyerman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Loft</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source>Evaluating Nonresponse in a Web-Enabled Survey on Health and Aging Presentation at the 2001 Conference of the American Association for Public Opinion Research</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Montreal, Canada</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burlingame</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Dunn</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lehman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Axman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Earnshaw</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Rees</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Selection of Outcome Assessment Instruments for Inpatients With Severe and Persistent Mental Illness</article-title><source>Psychiatric Services</source><year>2005</year><volume>56</volume><fpage>444</fpage><lpage>451</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15812095</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1176/appi.ps.56.4.444</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Snoeker</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>van den Bogaard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Garretsen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Zinloze herhaling van informatie? Een exploratieve studie naar de informatieoverdracht binnen de GGZ. [Useless repetition of information? An explorative study on information processing in mental health care]</article-title><source>Maandblad Geestelijke Volksgezondheid</source><year>2006</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>112</fpage><lpage>119</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>